From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: read the chanctx of the throughput estimate under RCU

sta_estimate_expected_throughput() (361) reads
vif.bss_conf.chanctx_conf with rcu_dereference(), but its callers hold
the wiphy mutex, not the RCU read lock: a station dump
(nl80211_dump_station -> sta_set_sinfo) makes lockdep report
"suspicious rcu_dereference_check() usage" at that line. Only the band
is taken from the chanctx, so read it inside rcu_read_lock().

The same code is in OpenWrt main.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/sta_info.c
@@ -3001,9 +3001,11 @@
 	u32 duration;
 	u8 band = 0;
 
+	rcu_read_lock();
 	conf = rcu_dereference(sdata->vif.bss_conf.chanctx_conf);
 	if (conf)
 			band = conf->def.chan->band;
+	rcu_read_unlock();
 
 	duration = ieee80211_rate_expected_tx_airtime(hw, NULL, ri, band, true, 1024);
 	duration += duration >> 4; /* add assumed packet error rate of ~6% */
